# The compiler of language 3 (23.9, part 2), a program of the chain (languages 1-3). stdin: a text of language 3 (the subset
# of tower/l3ctext.py) and a zero byte; stdout: a text of language 2 with labels and a zero byte (the tool programs/l2l.tw reads
# it, twice: `cat out out` is `text 0 text 0`). So: text of language 3 -> l3c -> l2l -> seed -> image. The layout is serial: a
# row of the text is a layer of its own (the row and the jump to the next layer), nothing is packed (the planner of 23.10 comes
# later); A is 20, P is 2. The reference in Python, the words, the errors and the layout are in tower/l3ctext.py; this text
# does the same on the chain and a test compares the bytes. The text of this tool is in the subset itself (data and tables
# first, names of blocks a-z 0-9 _, no hex numbers), so that part 3 can have the tool compile itself.
# How it reads: a character at a time (key); a token is a name (a word), :name (a label), a number, "string", &name[lo:hi];
# a word with its arguments is carried out when the last argument has come. Tokens end at a blank or the zero byte.
# Tables made by tower/l3ctext.py (tables_text) stand between the marks "begin generated" and "end generated".

